{"id":"s2.2.11","slug":"trigonometric-values","title":"Trigonometric Values","content":"<p class=\"mb-4\">Trigonometry problems test knowledge of sine, cosine, tangent, and their reciprocals (cosecant, secant, cotangent) for special angles (0°, 30°, 45°, 60°, 90°) and their variations in each quadrant. To find values in any quadrant, you need to know:</p><ol class=\"list-decimal pl-6 space-y-2 mb-4\"><li><strong>The Sign:</strong> Use the mnemonic \"All Students Take Calculus\" to remember which functions are positive in Quadrants I (All), II (Sin), III (Tan), and IV (Cos).</li><li><strong>The Reference Angle:</strong> Convert the angle to its equivalent in the first quadrant to find the base value. For an angle θ: Q-I is θ, Q-II is 180°-θ, Q-III is θ-180°, Q-IV is 360°-θ.</li></ol><p>Familiarity with both degrees and radians (π = 180°) is necessary.</p>","summary":"Trigonometry problems test knowledge of sine, cosine, tangent, and their reciprocals (cosecant, secant, cotangent) for special angles (0°, 30°, 45°, 6","generation_guideline":"Generate a problem that requires finding the value of a trigonometric function for a special angle in any quadrant.","questions":[{"id":1,"text":"Calculate sin(−30°).","answer":"-1/2","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":2,"text":"If cos θ = .375 then sec θ =","answer":"8/3","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":3,"text":"Calculate sin(3π).","answer":"0","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":4,"text":"Calculate tan(225°).","answer":"1","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":5,"text":"Calculate sin(sin⁻¹(1/2)).","answer":"1/2","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":6,"text":"If sin θ = −.1 then csc θ =","answer":"-10","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":7,"text":"Calculate sin(11π/6).","answer":"-1/2","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":8,"text":"Calculate cos(−5π).","answer":"-1","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":9,"text":"Convert π/18 to degrees.","answer":"10","kind":"exact","tags":["conversions"]},{"id":10,"text":"Calculate cos(sec⁻¹(3)).","answer":"1/3","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":11,"text":"Convert 5π/8 to degrees.","answer":"112.5","kind":"exact","tags":["conversions"]},{"id":12,"text":"Convert π/5 to degrees.","answer":"36","kind":"exact","tags":["conversions"]},{"id":13,"text":"Calculate cos(sin⁻¹(1)).","answer":"0","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":14,"text":"Calculate tan(−45°).","answer":"-1","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":15,"text":"Calculate sin(−π).","answer":"0","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":16,"text":"Calculate cos(−300°).","answer":"1/2","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":17,"text":"Calculate sin⁻¹(sin 1).","answer":"1","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":18,"text":"Calculate csc(−150°).","answer":"-2","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":19,"text":"Calculate sec(120°).","answer":"-2","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":20,"text":"Calculate tan(−225°).","answer":"-1","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":21,"text":"Convert 3π/5 to degrees.","answer":"108","kind":"exact","tags":["conversions"]},{"id":22,"text":"Calculate tan(315°).","answer":"-1","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":23,"text":"If 0° < x < 90° and tan x = cot x, x =","answer":"45","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":24,"text":"If 280° = kπ then k =","answer":"14/9","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":25,"text":"Calculate tan(5π/4).","answer":"1","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":26,"text":"If cos θ = .08333... then sec θ =","answer":"12","kind":"exact","tags":["repeating-decimals"]},{"id":27,"text":"Calculate sin(5π) + cos(5π).","answer":"-1","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":28,"text":"Calculate sec(60°).","answer":"2","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":29,"text":"If 12° = π/k, k =","answer":"15","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":30,"text":"If cos θ = −.25 then sec θ =","answer":"-4","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":31,"text":"Calculate tan²(60°).","answer":"3","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":32,"text":"Convert 1.25π to degrees.","answer":"225","kind":"exact","tags":["conversions"]},{"id":33,"text":"Calculate cot²(60°).","answer":"1/3","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":34,"text":"Calculate sin(cos⁻¹(√2/2)).","answer":"√2/2","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":35,"text":"Calculate cos(−3π) − sin(−3π).","answer":"-1","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":36,"text":"Calculate cos(−4π/3) + sin(−5π/6).","answer":"-1","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":37,"text":"Calculate 2 sin(120°) cos(30°).","answer":"1.5","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":38,"text":"Calculate cos(240°) − sin(150°).","answer":"-1","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":39,"text":"Calculate sin(cos⁻¹(√3/2)).","answer":"1/2","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":40,"text":"Calculate sin(cos⁻¹(1)).","answer":"0","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":41,"text":"If csc θ = −3, where 270° < θ < 300°, then sin θ =","answer":"-1/3","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":42,"text":"Calculate sin(−7π/6) − cos(−2π/3).","answer":"1","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":43,"text":"If sec θ = −3, and θ is in QIII, then cos θ =","answer":"-1/3","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":44,"text":"Calculate cos(5π/6) × sin(2π/3).","answer":"-3/4","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":45,"text":"Calculate sin(3π/4) × cos(5π/4).","answer":"-1/2","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":46,"text":"If sin 30° + cos 60° = tan x and 0° ≤ x ≤ 90°, x =","answer":"45","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":47,"text":"Calculate cos(sin⁻¹(√3/2)).","answer":"1/2","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":48,"text":"Calculate sin(−π/3) × sin(π/3).","answer":"-3/4","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":49,"text":"Calculate cos(120°) × cos(120°).","answer":"1/4","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":50,"text":"If 216° = kπ, k =","answer":"6/5","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":51,"text":"Calculate cos(−2π/3) × cos(4π/3).","answer":"1/4","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":52,"text":"Calculate tan(30°) × cot(60°).","answer":"1/3","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":53,"text":"Calculate cos(−π/3) × cos(π/3).","answer":"1/4","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":54,"text":"If sin(π/6) + cos(π/3) = tan(π/k), then k =","answer":"4","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":55,"text":"If cos⁻¹(.8) + cos⁻¹(.6) = kπ, then k =","answer":"1/2","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":56,"text":"Calculate sin(300°) × cos(330°).","answer":"-3/4","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":57,"text":"Calculate sin(−π/6) × cos(π/3).","answer":"-1/4","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":58,"text":"If 630° = kπ, k =","answer":"3.5","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]}]}